Reduced latency when monitoring (Segno: docs/design/recording.md §22).

A monitored track is heard sooner: EngineBehaviour::isMonitoredWithReducedLatency picks the tracks
played live whose output skips the edit's latency compensation (wrapped in an UncompensatedNode,
which a SummingNode sums as it is: not delayed to line up with its other inputs, and its own
latency doesn't delay them), and EngineBehaviour::shouldBypassWhileMonitoring the plugins left out
of such a track's own chain while it's monitored, without touching their enabled state. A rack
whose instances are all left out isn't built meanwhile, so its latency doesn't delay what it's
summed with. Renders never ask. With neither overridden, nothing changes.

